<BaseLayout title="About"><section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24"><p class="kicker">About / Boyuan (Ben) Wang</p><h1 class="text-4xl mt-6 mb-8">A bit about me.</h1><div class="prose"><p>I’m a mechanical engineering M.S. student at Duke, graduating in December 2026, and a graduate researcher in the General Robotics Lab. I earned my B.S. in Mechanical Engineering at Ohio State, with a minor in Computer and Information Science.</p><p>I like the part where a design becomes something you can put on a bench and try. A mechanism that moves well in CAD still has to be assembled, wired, controlled, and tested. That’s where much of my work happens.</p><p>I’m also interested in what a machine can learn from what it sees or hears. On the robotic hand project, I worked on the hardware, simulation, and control setup and helped get the visual inference pipeline running. For our intubation capstone, I built the testbed for studying acoustic signals from tube–tissue contact; my teammates worked on denoising and learning-based analysis.</p><p>Longer term, I’d like to build robots that help with everyday physical tasks, especially in elder care. For now, I’m learning by building the pieces and getting them to work together.</p><h2>Tools I work with</h2><p>SolidWorks, Fusion, GD&amp;T, Python, C++, URDF, PyBullet, MuJoCo, ROS / ROS 2, machining, rapid prototyping, soldering, and electromechanical system integration.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p><a href="mailto:bw277@duke.edu">bw277@duke.edu</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/boyuan-ben-wang/">LinkedIn</a></p></div></section></BaseLayout>
